From: KeegantheVeganat0r <58369898+KeegantheVeganat0r@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmdevapi: Skip Death Stranding code hooks on ARM64EC

The controller-output hooks overwrite Death Stranding's settings code with
calls that expect register-preserving x86-64 thunks: the settings-entry hook
must return the Wwise audio system in R8 and keep RCX/RDX intact, and the
UI-store hooks must perform the original store themselves.

Those thunks are assembled only for x86-64. On ARM64EC the fallback maps them
to the plain C functions, so the game resumes with clobbered registers and an
unperformed store. Applying any graphics setting then corrupts the settings
transaction (access violation at ds.exe+0x2DCBA00 or a stack-cookie fast-fail
at ds.exe+0x3B033D0).

Do not install the code hooks where the thunks are unavailable.
---
 dlls/mmdevapi/main.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/mmdevapi/main.c b/dlls/mmdevapi/main.c
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/main.c
@@ -545,6 +545,10 @@ static BOOL enable_death_stranding_controller_effects(void)
     if (GetEnvironmentVariableW(L"PROTON_DEATH_STRANDING_CONTROLLER_EFFECTS", value, ARRAY_SIZE(value)) != 1
             || value[0] != '1')
         return FALSE;
+#if !defined(__x86_64__) || defined(__arm64ec__)
+    WARN("Death Stranding controller output hooks are not supported on this architecture.\n");
+    return FALSE;
+#endif
     if (!(nt = RtlImageNtHeader(module))) return FALSE;
 
     section = IMAGE_FIRST_SECTION(nt);
-- 
